% RETRANSITION, bars 65-70 (Tempo I, 3/4). The E of the A minor bar slips to E flat (V of A flat).
% Horn 1 alone over the double basses' and timpani's E flat: the motto's tail E flat-D-D flat-C to B flat.

% c368: MIDI only: the strings' niente at 66 is on notes tied from 65; CC11 0.75 on the barline of 66 and 1.0 at 67 (barline steps only: bar 66 has no inner column, and a spacer ramp there changed the system's spacing, c300). Vln I rests 65-69, so the shared violin channel fades Vln II alone (Casanelles PDF 124, 142)
retrVlnOne = { R2.*5 | r2 es''8(\p^\markup \italic "espr." f''8 | }
% c398: Vln II and violas change bow on the tied note at 66: the slur from 64 b3 is an up-bow (pickup, Adler part 1 PDF 38 obs. 1) and the fade to niente a fresh down-bow, instead of about 10 s (64 b3-66 at crotchet 42/52) on one bow (Adler part 1 PDF 39: do not overload the bow in slow passages; PDF 38, Ex. II-20: down- and up-bow marked over the long note)
retrVlnTwo = { des'2.)~\pp | \once \override Staff.Hairpin.circled-tip = ##t \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.75 des'2.\>\downbow | \set Staff.midiExpression = #1.0 R2.*3\! | r2 es'8(\p^\markup \italic "sul D" f'8 | }  % c076: sul D, as at 22 (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 26: on a lower string go no higher than the fourth position, the octave or ninth; E flat5 is the ninth of D). Was sul G (c031)  % c096: "unis." dropped (after non div. there is no division to cancel; Adler part 1 PDF 30)
retrVla = { g2.)~\pp | \once \override Staff.Hairpin.circled-tip = ##t \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.75 g2.\>\downbow | \set Staff.midiExpression = #1.0 R2.*4\! | }  % c096: "unis., sul C" moved: sul C now at 64 b3 where the slur starts; 64 is non div., so no unis. is needed (Adler part 1 PDF 30, 64)
retrVc = { bes,2.~\pp | \once \override Staff.Hairpin.circled-tip = ##t \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.75 bes,2.\> | \set Staff.midiExpression = #1.0 R2.*4\! | }
% c300: MIDI only (nothing printed): the basses' held E flat2 (pp, 4 soli) rendered at velocity 50 against horn 1's p motto tail at 44-50 (67-69), so the pedal was the loudest line
% under the solo; CC11 steps to 0.88 at 66 and 0.75 at 67, on barlines so the spacing does not change (as the coda pedal 83-86, c240) and returns to 1.0 at 71 (aTwoCb). Sebesky PDF 240-241: compare the result with the intention; PDF 13-14: focus on the primary element
% c344: "sul A": the E flat2 pedal under horn 1's p solo on the A string (third position, inside the ninth-of-the-open-string limit), not the D string; the bass is "slightly duller on the two lower strings (E and A), and more penetrating on the upper ones (D and G)" (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 27; PDF 26 limit). Text only; score.midi unchanged (c300 CC11 kept)
retrCb = { es,2.\pp~^\markup \italic \override #'(baseline-skip . 2.4) \column { "4 soli, sul A," "change bow at will" } | \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.88 es,2.~ | \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.75 es,2.~ | es,2.~ | es,2.~ | es,2. | }
% c315: part-only cue for the harp before its entry at 71 after 14 bars' rest across poco allargando (60), Largamente (61), allargando (64) and Tempo I (65) (MOLA PDF 5, Ex. 4, PDF 10). Score: rests.
retrHarpR = { R2.*3 | \tag #'score { R2.*3 } \tag #'part { \cueDuring #"hnOneQ" #DOWN { <>^\markup \tiny "Hn. 1" R2.*3 } } | }
retrTimp = { R2.^\markup \small "soft sticks" | R2. | es2.:32\ppp~^\markup \small \italic "near the rim" | es2.:32~ | \once \override Staff.Hairpin.circled-tip = ##t es2.:32~\> | es2:32~ es8\! r8 | }  % c290: the roll fades to niente over 69-70 as Hn 1 falls to pp on B flat3, the same ending as the A flat roll at 2-3 (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 127: removing a timbre belongs to the diminuendo); answers c289 without shortening the roll  % c056: roll ends on a tied stroke with the horn and bassoons (Adler part 2 PDF 80, Ex. XII-47)  % c146: ppp roll near the rim, ord. at 79 (Adler part 2 PDF 80: "a beautiful pianissimo ... closer to the rim")
% c195: since c194's a2 at 61-62 the part-combiner prints soloText "1. solo" itself at 67; the score-tagged markup printed it a second time (removed)
retrHnOne = { R2.*2 | \set Staff.soloText = "1. solo" es'2.(\p\<-\tag #'part ^\markup \bold "solo"^\markup \italic "dolce" | d'4\mp\> des'4 c'4 | bes2.~ | bes2.)\pp | \set Staff.soloText = "1." }  % c343: B flat3 held to the barline, so the horn's last note coincides with the violins' pickup at 70 b3 (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 125-126, transfer of phrases; Dvorak 9/ii brass held into bar 101)  % c115: horn 2 is tacet, so 70's crotchet rest belongs to horn 1 alone and stays in the stave (Gould PDF 49, 51)  % c046: label written out: after horn 2's "2." at 61-62 the part-combiner no longer prints it  % c035: one label, "1. solo"
retrHnTwo = { R2.*5 | \tag #'score s2. \tag #'part R2. | }  % c115: horn 2 tacet; in the score bar 70 is a spacer so horn 1's crotchet rest is the only rest and stays in the stave (Gould PDF 49, 51)
% c043: bassoon 1 enters at 68 a third under horn 1's tail (D-D flat-C over B flat-B flat-A flat), so the tail over the held dominant is the
% 8-7-6-5 / 6-5-4-3 progression and 68 b3 is a passing 6/4 (A flat-C over E flat) into V7 at 69 (A&S PDF 311-314, Ex. 19-14, 19-16).
retrBsnOne = { R2.*3 | \tweak Stem.direction #DOWN bes2(\pp-\tag #'score ^\markup \bold "1." \tweak Stem.direction #DOWN aes4 | g2.) | g2.-\tweak stencil ##f \pp( | }  % c160: hidden dynamic for MIDI only: this voice had no dynamic of its own, so score.midi played it at LilyPond's default volume 0.71 (louder than ff) against the printed mark (Sebesky PDF 240-241: compare the score with the recorded result)
% c377: bassoons hold G3/D flat3 through 70 b3 and resolve G3-A flat3 (Bsn 1) and D flat3-C3 (Bsn 2) into 71: contrary semitone convergence at the return, as at 30 and 82 (A&S PDF 563-566, 580 no. 6); fills the 70 b3 gap (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 125)
retrBsnTwo = { R2.*4 | des2.\pp | des2.-\tweak stencil ##f \pp \breathe | }  % c416: breath at 70/71 (69-74 b2 was about 19.6 s at pp with no rest); covered by bassoon 1's tied G3-A flat3 and the basses' E flat2 (Adler part 1 PDF 175, 188, 230)  % c160: hidden dynamic for MIDI only: this voice had no dynamic of its own, so score.midi played it at LilyPond's default volume 0.71 (louder than ff) against the printed mark (Sebesky PDF 240-241: compare the score with the recorded result)
% c145: the "1." player labels at 67-68 are score-only; a single player's part does not carry the shared-staff label (Adler part 2 PDF 301, Ex. XVIII-10b: the parts drop the score's "1."); Horn 1 keeps "solo"
